---
title: Neapolitan Refrigerator Sheet Cake
author: Barbara Muirhead
category: Desserts
source: Loving Memories of Mildred
---

@cake mix{1%pkg}
@Jell-O (4 serving size){1%pkg}
@boiling water{0.75%cup}
@cold water{1%cup}
@Dream Whip{1%envelop}
@instant pudding{1%small pkg}
@cold milk{1.5%cups}
@vanilla{1%tsp}

Bake cake mix in 9x13 pan. Dissolve Jell-O in 3/4 cup boiling water. Add one cup cold water and set aside. Once cake has cooled, poke holes deep through top of cake about 1 inch apart and slowly pour Jell-O mix into the holes. Refrigerate cake.

==Topping==
Mix envelop of Dream Whip, instant pudding, cold milk and vanilla until stiff. Immediately frost cake. Store in refrigerator. (Especially good with lime Jell-O and lemon pudding)
